  "body": "Found while fixing #1504 (PR #1522), beside #1503 (PR #1513).\n\nWhat happens: two laws now confine an endpoint-and-width slot to its picks.\n- `machining2d::slot_room::SlotBound` (PR #1522, plain Slot) reads two opposite straight edges or one face/ring. It seeds the fit and refuses, with numbers, a slot too wide, too long or past the picks.\n- `operation::slot_fit::refuse_unfit_slot` (PR #1513, Trochoidal slot) is a capsule-in-region law over the picked region. Its region comes from `selection_region`, which refuses open edge runs, so a Trochoidal slot picked by two edges is refused before the law runs.\n\nExpected: one law that both kinds call. Two ways to get there: the Trochoidal slot reads its picks through `operation::slot_bound_of` and calls `SlotBound::confine`, or `refuse_unfit_slot` becomes a thin wrapper over it. Then both kinds accept edge picks, refuse with the same messages and use one tolerance (`FIT_TOL` 0.01 mm on one side, 1e-4 mm on the other).\n\nDone means: one confine function called by both slot arms; a Trochoidal slot picked by two opposite edges is fitted or refused by name exactly like a Slot; the pins of #1504 and #1503 still pass.\n",
